    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0774" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg678"/>

                <head>No. 69.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokei</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic">the</hi>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1879-07-14">14<hi rendition="#italic">th
                                July</hi>, 1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the same:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my letters Nos. 65, 67,
                    and 68, with regard to the German steamer Hesperia, to which I have as yet
                    received no reply, I have the honor to inform your excellency that I shall now
                    order the said steamer, which has been kept in quarantine for three days and a
                    half without consent from the German authorities, to proceed forthwith to
                    Yokohama, its place of destination.</p>
                <p>With the assurance of my most distinguished consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed>VON EISENDECHER.</signed></closer>




